          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভ্যান — bhæn — \"a van; a cycle van\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "একটা ভ্যান আমাদের মালপত্র স্টেশনে নিয়ে গেল। ekṭā bhæn āmāder mālpôtrô sṭeshône niye gelô. A van took our luggage to the station."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In a small town a ভ্যান (bhæn) is often a pedalled tricycle with a flat wooden bed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ভ্যান (bhæn) is borrowed from English van; Bengali has no v, so the word begins with ভ, and the y-phala gives the English vowel æ."
            }
          ]
        },
