          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দৌড়ানো — douṛāno — \"to race; to run fast\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অরুণ দৌড়ে বাসে উঠল। ôrun douṛe bāse uṭhlô. Arun ran and got on the bus."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি দৌড়ালেন, tini douṛālen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The -এ form দৌড়ে is the one you hear most: দৌড়ে এল, came running."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first vowel sign is ৌ, the vowel ou."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দৌড়ানো (douṛāno) is inherited: CDIAL lists Bengali dauṛā and dauṛāna, \"to run\", under Sanskrit drávati, \"runs\" (CDIAL 6624), and notes that the word probably came east from the languages to the west."
            }
          ]
        },
